  "term": "cyclic AMP",
  "definition": "Cyclic AMP (cAMP) is a cell signaling molecule produced by transmembrane and soluble adenylyl cyclases. In neurons, it helps carry signals within localized cellular microdomains and can drive downstream processes such as protein kinase A activation and regulation of neurite growth.",
